@*
    A game's title as a scoreboard: away over home, each team's mark and name with its score
    trailing. It replaced a sentence ("● Steelers 16 at ● Saints 10") in which the names and the
    figures were one run of title type and nothing said who won. Here the score is the largest
    thing on the line, and when a game is over the loser's row drops to secondary ink at regular
    weight, so the winner reads heavier without a word. Live and tied games keep both rows at
    full weight: nobody has lost yet, or nobody did.

    It sits inside PanelTitle's h2, which takes phrasing content only, so every part is a span:
    the two-row shape is CSS (a grid whose rows are subgrids, so both scores share one right
    edge). The marks and the links' shortcuts are hidden from assistive tech, and a hidden
    separator joins the rows, so the heading still says "Pittsburgh Steelers 16, New Orleans
    Saints 10" — or "… at …" before a ball is thrown. Spaces between parts are written as
    expressions because Razor drops whitespace-only text around markup; a grid or flex
    container ignores them, a screen reader does not.

    Before a game starts there is no score and nothing trails the rows: the start time is the
    title's Detail line, once. Compact is the same parts on one line, for the wager header:
    "away · at · home" at --text-title3 throughout, the middots hidden from assistive tech.
*@

@{
    // A fight has a winner, not a score (ADR 0021): the loser still drops to secondary ink, and
    // the 1–0 that records the result is left unprinted — the title's detail line says how it ended.
    var hasScore = Scoreline.Has(Game) && !FightSports.IsFight(Game.Sport?.Key);
    var loser = Loser;
    var joiner = FightSports.IsFight(Game.Sport?.Key) ? "vs" : "at";
}

<span class="scoreboard@(Compact ? " scoreboard--compact" : "")">
    @Row(Game.AwayTeamId, Game.AwayTeam, "Away", Game.AwayScore, hasScore, loser == Side.Away)
    @if (Compact)
    {
        <span class="scoreboard__at" aria-hidden="true">·</span>@(" ")<span class="scoreboard__at">@joiner</span>@(" ")<span class="scoreboard__at" aria-hidden="true">·</span>
    }
    else
    {
        <span class="sr-only">@(hasScore ? ", " : $" {joiner} ")</span>
    }
    @Row(Game.HomeTeamId, Game.HomeTeam, "Home", Game.HomeScore, hasScore, loser == Side.Home)
</span>

@code {
    /// <summary>The game whose two teams and score this draws.</summary>
    [Parameter, EditorRequired] public Game Game { get; set; } = default!;

    /// <summary>A team's name was pressed; carries that team's id so the host can open its window.</summary>
    [Parameter] public EventCallback<int> OnTeam { get; set; }

    /// <summary>One line at <c>--text-title3</c> instead of two stacked rows.</summary>
    [Parameter] public bool Compact { get; set; }

    private enum Side { None, Away, Home }

    // Only a finished game has a loser, and only when the scores differ: an NFL tie has none.
    private Side Loser => Game.Status == GameStatus.Final && Scoreline.Has(Game)
        ? (Game.AwayScore ?? 0).CompareTo(Game.HomeScore ?? 0) switch
        {
            < 0 => Side.Away,
            > 0 => Side.Home,
            _ => Side.None,
        }
        : Side.None;

    private RenderFragment Row(int teamId, Team? team, string fallback, int? score, bool hasScore, bool isLoser) => __builder =>
    {
        <span class="scoreboard__row@(isLoser ? " scoreboard__row--loser" : "")">
            <span class="scoreboard__name">
                <TeamMark Sport="@Game.Sport?.Key" Abbrev="@team?.Abbrev" Size="TeamMarkSize.Large" />
                <DeskLink Destination="team" Icon="@Icons.Material.Filled.Shield"
                          OnClick="() => OnTeam.InvokeAsync(teamId)">
                    @(team?.Name ?? fallback)
                </DeskLink>
            </span>
            @if (hasScore)
            {
                @(" ")<span class="scoreboard__score">@(score ?? 0)</span>
            }
        </span>
    };
}
